{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1493112-new-to-exalted-where-do-i-even-start","id":1493112,"title":"New to Exalted, where do I even start?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-15T07:39:25-07:00","id":1493112,"title":"New to Exalted, where do I even start?","content":"As the title states, I have very little to any idea of what I'm doing. I was going to be running a solo campaign to start, with a friend of mine who's more experienced in Exalted to GM, but I have no idea where to start with just about anything else. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have any suggestions for getting into Exalted? What kinds of characters are recommended for a new player to play, to get an idea of how the game handles? What about books and such; my friend has the basic 3rd Edition book, but what other books can help me get into the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T09:18:57-07:00","id":1493116,"title":"","content":"Depends on how deep you want to get into things. The core book is all you <i>technically</i> need to play the game, but there are a number of factors that could determine what you might want to buy:<br /> <br /> 1. Are you playing a Solar Exalt, or one of the other Exalted types? The Solar Exalted are the &quot;default&quot; character type, and are fully explained within the core book. However, if you want to play as one of the other Exalt types, then you'll need to purchase their books as well. For Dragon-Blooded that would be &quot;What Fire Has Wrought&quot; and for Lunars that would be &quot;Fangs at the Gates.&quot; Sidereals and other types of Exalted are currently not officially available, though there's a lot of homebrew floating around. Still, for a first time player official material would probably be best.<br /> <br /> 2. Do you want to know more about the location your campaign will take place in? Exalted has 5 &quot;Directions&quot; that constitute the major regions of the game. Currently, only the Center Direction has been detailed in 3rd Edition via the book &quot;The Realm.&quot; For the other directions (North, South, East, West), you'll need to purchase one of the 2nd edition books, in the series &quot;Compass of Terrestrial Directions.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Do you want more options for play, such as more Charms and Artifacts? For the latter, I would recommend Arms of the Chosen. The former depends on what type of Exalt you're playing. The Lunar Companion book, which would have additional options for them, is currently unreleased. The Solar Companion book &quot;Miracles of the Solar Exalted&quot; is... not the greatest quality in terms of material. Really, only the Dragon-Blooded Companion &quot;Heirs of the Shogunate&quot; is worth getting if you're playing that type of Exalt.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}